WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.862 --> 00:00:15.622
get out of here!"

2
00:00:15.843 --> 00:00:16.563
Zann exclaimed.

3
00:00:16.583 --> 00:00:23.749
"Hurry!" He and Perda yanked the others back through the wormhole before it could swirl shut behind them.

4
00:00:23.789 --> 00:00:26.191
Zann was relieved when they were back in the vortex.

5
00:00:27.852 --> 00:00:29.834
"That was close," Perda said.

6
00:00:29.854 --> 00:00:32.136
"Yeah," Zann agreed.

7
00:00:32.768 --> 00:00:34.830
"But what if Wyssa is in Fardark?

8
00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:35.831
Or Morb?"

9
00:00:35.851 --> 00:00:41.776
"That definitely looked like the kind of place where they would hang out," Gliss said with a shudder.

10
00:00:41.796 --> 00:00:44.158
"It doesn't matter," Darb said.

11
00:00:44.178 --> 00:00:46.199
"It was too risky to stay."

12
00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:48.381
"Right," Perda agreed.

13
00:00:48.401 --> 00:00:53.866
"And if Morb and Wyssa had gone there, they probably would have moved on by now anyway.

14
00:00:54.867 --> 00:00:57.049
Nobody would stay in Fardark for long."

15
00:00:58.650 --> 00:00:59.731
Zann thought of something.

16
00:00:59.751 --> 00:01:02.913
"Actually, we know my parents aren't there.

17
00:01:03.873 --> 00:01:06.755
The skies in Fardark are dark, not blue.

18
00:01:07.555 --> 00:01:12.357
Plus, Perda and I didn't see any creatures small enough to live in those tiny houses."

19
00:01:12.377 --> 00:01:16.679
"Are you sure your dreams are showing you where your parents are?"

20
00:01:16.959 --> 00:01:18.199
Darb sounded dubious.

21
00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:23.542
Zann had told his friends about his latest dream while they all walked back to the wormhole in

22
00:01:23.562 --> 00:01:28.904
Chronos. "The more dreams I have, the more sure I am," Zann replied.

23
00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:32.642
"I think the images are coming from my message stone.

24
00:01:33.523 --> 00:01:38.466
The most realistic dream I had was when we were resting in Wyssa's home world."

25
00:01:39.527 --> 00:01:40.788
He remembered something else.

26
00:01:40.808 --> 00:01:46.932
"Also, I bet that was Wyssa's world we passed the time I had the waking dream!

27
00:01:47.392 --> 00:01:55.658
Remember? All I saw through that wormhole were some trees with purple leaves—just like the ones in Wyssa's

28
00:01:55.698 --> 00:01:58.160
world!" Gliss looked confused.

29
00:01:58.596 --> 00:02:01.117
"So we passed Wyssa's world twice?"

30
00:02:01.137 --> 00:02:05.798
"Yeah. Perda and I ended up in Fardark twice too."

31
00:02:06.338 --> 00:02:06.979
Zann shrugged.

32
00:02:06.999 --> 00:02:10.340
"That does seem weird, now that I think about it."

33
00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:12.981
"Not really," Perda said.

34
00:02:13.001 --> 00:02:17.682
"I did some research on the vortex back in Swamp Bottom, and—" "You did?"

35
00:02:18.002 --> 00:02:18.702
Zann broke in.

36
00:02:19.543 --> 00:02:20.563
Perda shot him a look.

37
00:02:21.103 --> 00:02:23.704
"I told you I was thinking about becoming an explorer.

38
00:02:24.584 --> 00:02:30.769
I started preparing by reading all your parents' books, including the one called Voyages Through the Vortex."

39
00:02:30.789 --> 00:02:35.513
"Oh." Zann was surprised she had read all of those books.

40
00:02:36.634 --> 00:02:37.635
"What did you find out?"

41
00:02:37.655 --> 00:02:40.778
"Haven't you read your parents' books, Zann?"

42
00:02:40.958 --> 00:02:41.559
Gliss asked.

43
00:02:41.579 --> 00:02:44.701
"Sure. I mean, some of them."

44
00:02:44.982 --> 00:02:46.443
Zann shrugged sheepishly.

45
00:02:46.463 --> 00:02:52.368
"Actually, I've mostly just looked at the pictures of the cool monsters and stuff.

46
00:02:53.148 --> 00:02:55.690
They wrote the vortex book when I was really young."

47
00:02:55.710 --> 00:03:01.653
"The vortex isn't like a regular road or tunnel or anything like that," Perda explained.

48
00:03:01.673 --> 00:03:07.256
"It's just a magical space between worlds that's always shifting in unpredictable ways.

49
00:03:08.357 --> 00:03:10.398
Nobody knows exactly how it works.

50
00:03:11.338 --> 00:03:16.981
That's why it's important to have an experienced guide like Wyssa if you're not experienced yourself.

51
00:03:18.502 --> 00:03:21.404
You also need strong magic to help you navigate.

52
00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:26.163
Otherwise you can get yourself in trouble—at least that's what the book said."

53
00:03:27.084 --> 00:03:29.966
"Your parents must have pretty strong magic, huh, Zann?"

54
00:03:30.227 --> 00:03:30.747
Gliss said.

55
00:03:30.767 --> 00:03:32.849
"Even though they're not Reds?"

56
00:03:32.869 --> 00:03:38.013
"Yeah. Plus they have lots of experience traveling between worlds."

57
00:03:38.994 --> 00:03:42.297
But for once Zann wasn't really thinking about his parents.

58
00:03:43.417 --> 00:03:45.419
Perda's words had reminded him of Venna.

59
00:03:45.819 --> 00:03:47.321
She'd had very strong magic.

60
00:03:48.201 --> 00:03:51.144
But she'd been under a Dousing spell when she fell into the wormhole.

61
00:03:51.508 --> 00:03:52.449
What had become of her?

62
00:03:53.389 --> 00:03:56.632
He pushed the thought aside, realizing that Perda was still talking.

63
00:03:57.592 --> 00:04:02.015
"So there's no way to predict which wormhole we'll pass next," she was saying.

64
00:04:02.035 --> 00:04:05.198
"The next one could lead back into Magica.

65
00:04:06.398 --> 00:04:08.740
Or it could take us into Fardark yet again.

66
00:04:09.741 --> 00:04:14.464
Or into a brand-new world—maybe even one that's never been discovered before."

67
00:04:14.484 --> 00:04:17.666
"Or World X," Zann murmured.

68
00:04:17.686 --> 00:04:20.168
"Let me get this straight."

69
00:04:20.512 --> 00:04:21.613
Gliss sounded worried.

70
00:04:21.633 --> 00:04:26.437
"We have no way of finding a wormhole back into Magica?"

71
00:04:27.278 --> 00:04:28.018
Perda shrugged.

72
00:04:28.038 --> 00:04:29.860
"Not unless we get lucky."

73
00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:32.662
"Or find Wyssa," Darb said.

74
00:04:32.682 --> 00:04:34.703
"Or somebody else who can guide us."

75
00:04:35.684 --> 00:04:36.645
"Like my parents."

76
00:04:37.286 --> 00:04:39.187
Zann felt a tingling on his forehead.

77
00:04:40.008 --> 00:04:41.449
The marks were glowing again.

78
00:04:41.469 --> 00:04:43.070
"Hold on!"

79
00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:45.412
he said, reaching for the next wormhole.

80
00:04:46.313 --> 00:04:50.096
As he grabbed the wormhole’s edge, he caught a glimpse of blue sky.

81
00:04:50.976 --> 00:04:52.517
He tried not to get too excited though.

82
00:04:53.418 --> 00:04:56.501
Lots of worlds, including Magica, had blue skies.

83
00:04:57.441 --> 00:04:59.383
Still, he couldn't help hoping.

84
00:05:00.724 --> 00:05:03.446
Splash! "Drat—glurb!"

85
00:05:04.007 --> 00:05:06.669
Zann gurgled as he felt himself sinking under water.

86
00:05:06.689 --> 00:05:08.770
"Oh no," he thought.

87
00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:11.192
"Did we land in Skellia again?"

88
00:05:12.073 --> 00:05:16.537
But he quickly realized that this water was much calmer than the rough seas of Skellia.

89
00:05:17.417 --> 00:05:21.024
It was also much cooler than the boiling lake in Drac.

90
00:05:21.044 --> 00:05:24.908
When Zann came up for air, his friends were bobbing in the water nearby.

91
00:05:24.928 --> 00:05:26.869
"Where are we?"

92
00:05:27.190 --> 00:05:30.052
Zann asked, pushing a clump of wet hair out of his eyes.

93
00:05:30.072 --> 00:05:32.374
"I don't know," Gliss said.

94
00:05:32.394 --> 00:05:33.855
"But it looks nice."

95
00:05:35.016 --> 00:05:37.358
They were in the middle of a large, tranquil lake.

96
00:05:38.239 --> 00:05:43.003
Pretty silver and gold fish darted around, nibbling at the swaying water grasses.

97
00:05:44.104 --> 00:05:48.048
On shore a green lawn sloped gently up to a lush forest.

98
00:05:49.020 --> 00:05:54.082
A gleaming city of elegant spires and towers stood atop a hill in the distance.

99
00:05:55.583 --> 00:06:01.265
When Zann and his friends swam to shore, they heard birds singing and felt a warm, gentle breeze.

100
00:06:02.286 --> 00:06:04.947
The ground was soft and springy beneath Zann's feet.

101
00:06:06.147 --> 00:06:08.388
He snapped his fingers to conjure dry clothes.

102
00:06:09.329 --> 00:06:11.890
"Good. Our magic works here," he said.

103
00:06:12.750 --> 00:06:14.211
He touched his hair to dry it.

104
00:06:14.231 --> 00:06:16.592
"I just have one question.

105
00:06:16.996 --> 00:06:20.478
Why are so many of the wormholes located over water?"

106
00:06:22.039 --> 00:06:23.140
Darb started to laugh.

107
00:06:23.640 --> 00:06:27.863
Then he stopped, leaning closer to stare at Zann's forehead.

108
00:06:27.883 --> 00:06:30.124
"Uh-oh," he said.

109
00:06:30.144 --> 00:06:32.226
"Zann, your face is clean!"

110
00:06:32.246 --> 00:06:34.867
"Gee, thanks," Zann said.

111
00:06:34.887 --> 00:06:36.969
"Yours looks pretty clean too."

112
00:06:37.809 --> 00:06:38.590
Perda gasped.

113
00:06:38.610 --> 00:06:39.770
"No, Zann.

114
00:06:40.211 --> 00:06:41.331
This is a problem!"

115
00:06:41.552 --> 00:06:41.992
she cried.

116
00:06:42.936 --> 00:06:47.080
"When your head went under water, Wyssa's fingerprints must have washed off.

117
00:06:48.141 --> 00:06:50.664
We have no way of tracking her anymore!"
